  "id": "COMPOUND:38022 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "The compound (1S,9S)-4,13-dimethoxy-17-methyl-17-azatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.010,15]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10,12,14-hexaene-3,12-diol appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets. This interaction is mediated via the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including Bezerramycin B, Sid124895033, and Isoerysenegalensein E. These compounds are all capable of binding to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a common mechanism of action that involves the recruitment of the complex to DNA. The evidence suggests that the compound may exert its effects by modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn influences DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for this compound in regulating DNA polymerase iota activity, possibly through the modulation of chromatin structure or other epigenetic processes.",
